  "narrative": "Independent validation for the EGFR-amplification association with dependency_EGFR (H4) does not support accepting the claim. Discovery R4, signed to the negative-dependency hypothesis, was positive and slightly larger than the approximate 10% relative-difference threshold, but its 95% interval remained very close to zero. Independent validation R13 is signed negative, with a wide interval including zero and both clinically meaningful positive and negative ranges. The two evidence sources are inconsistent, and the validated data do not provide a stable clinically meaningful association; I therefore keep H4 unresolved but close the direct investigation rather than accept it. This does not prove absence; a subgroup effect could remain hidden, so I registered an interaction test between EGFR amplification and KRAS wild-type status.\n\nI also reassessed the reversed KEAP1-loss claim H13. The parent discovery R7 was enormous relative to the NFE2L2 outcome scale: KEAP1-loss cells showed substantially less negative dependency_NFE2L2 than non-loss cells, with the 95% interval entirely on the side of clinically meaningful effect. This strongly supports the reversed dataset-specific association H13, even though the original mechanistic direction H7 was rejected. I accepted H13 and closed its direct investigation.\n\nI reassessed MYC-amplification versus POLR2A dependency H9. Its signed estimate is tiny and the upper confidence limit is below the approximate 10% relative threshold, so I rejected it as not supporting a clinically meaningful difference.\n\nCurrent supported dataset-specific findings are: MSI-high cells have much stronger WRN dependency; SMARCA4-loss cells have much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; and KEAP1-loss cells have much weaker NFE2L2 dependency. Current negative findings include rejected KRAS-mutation effects on BRAF dependency, BRAF V600E on BRAF dependency, EGFR amplification on STAT3 dependency, TP53-loss effect on MDM2 dependency in the original direction, and MYC amplification effect on POLR2A dependency. Current unresolved uncertainty includes KRAS mutation on KRAS dependency, ERBB2 amplification on ERBB2 dependency, TP53 loss on MDM2 dependency, MYC amplification on USP7 dependency, and EGFR amplification on EGFR dependency. The next analyses focus on heterogeneity of the three strong effects across lineage subtype and constructed research markers, plus one mechanistic EGFR/KRAS subgroup interaction.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted dataset-specific associations: H11 MSI-high stronger WRN dependency; H12 SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H13 KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency (reversal from H7). Rejected/not supported: H2, H3, H5, H7, H9, and H4 as a stable direct EGFR-amplification/EGFR-dependency claim? H4 currently unresolved but closed direct investigation. Unresolved active: H1 KRAS mutation on KRAS dependency, H6 ERBB2 amplification on ERBB2 dependency, H8 TP53 loss on MDM2 dependency, H10 MYC amplification on USP7 dependency. H4 validation inconsistent: discovery positive borderline, validation negative wide; keep unresolved uncertainty. Next analyses registered: interactions of accepted WRN, SMARCA2, and NFE2L2 effects with lineage_subtype and research markers D/E/F; direct marker associations with those three outcomes; EGFR-amplification effect within KRAS wild-type as interaction to explore failed replication. Future possible validations: if accepted effects need generalization or if marker interactions are large, request independent validation in later appraise. Maintain caution: causal claims and generalizability beyond this dataset remain unavailable."
}

