  "narrative": "The new adenocarcinoma-restricted direct tests strongly confirm the three already accepted dataset-specific dependency associations. For MSI-high versus WRN in adenocarcinoma, the signed estimate is +0.784 with a narrow 95% interval [0.748, 0.821], far exceeding an approximate 10% threshold based on the WRN score scale; I accept H25 as a dataset-specific subgroup association. For SMARCA4-loss versus SMARCA2 in adenocarcinoma, the signed estimate is +0.775 [0.752, 0.798], again a very large and precise association; I accept H26. For KEAP1-loss versus weaker NFE2L2 dependency in adenocarcinoma, the signed estimate is +0.795 [0.769, 0.820], accepting H27 as the same reversed KEAP1/NFE2L2 relationship seen in the full eligible sample.\n\nThe lineage-subtype interaction tests mostly do not show strong evidence that the main effects differ between adenocarcinoma and non-adenocarcinoma cells. H15 rejects an SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 subtype interaction because the signed interval excludes clinically meaningful support in the claimed direction. H14 and H16 have signed point estimates near zero or opposite to the claimed direction, but their intervals include clinically meaningful values in the claimed direction, so I keep them unresolved but deferred rather than claiming precise absence. These are same-dataset subgroup contrasts, not independent validation, and they involve multiplicity and uneven cell sizes.\n\nLibrary ky context tests are informative. H28 shows no clinically meaningful ky interaction for MSI-high/WRN because the signed interval excludes meaningful support in the claimed direction; reject and close. H30 for KEAP1/NFE2L2 is near zero and opposite to the claimed direction, though imprecise, so I leave it unresolved but deferred. H29 is the one notable borderline finding: the signed SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 ky interaction is +0.044 [ -0.003, 0.091], just around the approximate 10% SMARCA2 scale threshold. The interval crosses zero and includes both negligible and meaningful values, so it cannot support a stable library-context modification; I keep H29 active and propose a direct ky-subgroup SMARCA2 test to clarify it. I also propose direct ky tests for WRN and NFE2L2 to interpret the small imprecise ky interaction estimates.\n\nThe EGFR-amplification interaction within KRAS wild-type cells, H20, does not support the failed direct EGFR dependency signal: the signed estimate is small and opposite, though the interval is wide enough to include a clinically meaningful effect in the claimed direction. Given the earlier inconsistent validation for H4, I defer further EGFR subgroup work. ARID1A-loss versus SMARCA2 dependency is negligible, H34, and KEAP1-loss versus USP7 dependency, H35, is small and imprecise; both remain unresolved only because intervals include some clinically meaningful values, but they are low priority. I request independent validation for H11 because MSI-high/WRN is a large, mechanistically meaningful synthetic-lethal signal with relatively small MSI-high exposure count in discovery, and external validation would strengthen the accepted association. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal claims or guaranteed generalizable findings.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted robust dataset-specific dependency associations: H11/H25 MSI-high stronger WRN dependency; H12/H26 SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H13/H27 KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency. Direct adenocarcinoma estimates are large and precise. Context interactions: lineage subtype mostly null for SMARCA2 (H15 rejected); WRN/NFE2L2 subtype interactions unresolved but low priority. Ky library: WRN interaction rejected (H28); NFE2L2 interaction unresolved low priority (H30); SMARCA2 ky interaction borderline (H29), active and direct ky tests proposed. EGFR/KRAS-WT interaction H20 unresolved but low priority after inconsistent H4 validation. ARID1A/SMARCA2 H34 and KEAP1/USP7 H35 remain unresolved but deferred. Pending validation requested: H11 MSI-high WRN. Next analyses: direct ky subgroup tests for WRN, SMARCA2, NFE2L2; pending registered marker interactions and culture interactions may be useful if budget allows. Maintain multiplicity caution and no causal/generalizability claims without validation.",
  "validate": "H11"
}

