  "narrative": "The new direct context tests strongly support the three previously accepted dependency associations. For SMARCA4-loss versus dependency_SMARCA2 within the Ky library, R27 is signed to the negative-dependency hypothesis and is +0.814 with a 95% interval [0.774, 0.855]. This is far above a conservative ~10% score-scale benchmark and resolves the earlier borderline Ky interaction by showing that the main SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 effect remains very large inside Ky cells. For MSI-high versus dependency_WRN within Ky, R28 is +0.751 [0.693, 0.809]; although the exposed Ky/MSI-high cell has only 27 observations, the lower bound remains enormous, so I accept it as a dataset-specific context association while noting small-cell caution. For KEAP1-loss versus weaker NFE2L2 dependency within Ky, R29 is +0.787 [0.741, 0.832]. The adherent-culture direct tests are similarly strong: WRN/MSI-high +0.816 [0.784, 0.849], SMARCA2/SMARCA4-loss +0.786 [0.762, 0.810], and NFE2L2/KEAP1-loss +0.795 [0.770, 0.820]. I accept H36-H41 as dataset-specific within-context associations supporting the robustness of the accepted trio, not as independent validation.\n\nThe most important new mechanistic result is TP53 loss versus dependency_USP7. With direction +1, a positive signed estimate means TP53-loss cells have less negative USP7 dependency scores, i.e., weaker USP7 dependency. R38 is +0.804 [0.783, 0.825], an extremely large and precise dataset-specific association. It is mechanistically plausible because USP7 functions in p53/MDM2-related regulation, and TP53 loss could reduce reliance on USP7; however, this remains only an association in the supplied data. I accept H48 and keep it active, with context follow-up proposed before deciding whether it should become a leading validated claim.\n\nThe other new mechanistic tests are mostly null or imprecise. KRAS mutation versus dependency_RIT1, R33, is +0.003 with interval [-0.016, 0.023]; the upper bound is below the approximate 10% RIT1 score-scale benchmark, so I reject H42. BRAF V600E versus RIT1, R34, and ERBB2 amplification versus RIT1, R35, are near zero but have wide intervals that touch borderline clinically meaningful values in their claimed directions; H43 and H44 remain unresolved but deferred because the point estimates are negligible and the RIT1 panel otherwise gives little support. MYC amplification versus DHX9, R36, is near null with a borderline negative lower bound, so H46 is unresolved but deferred. TP53 loss versus RPL11, R37, is also near null with a borderline positive upper bound, so H47 is unresolved but deferred.\n\nI request independent validation for H12. The central SMARCA4-loss/dependency_SMARCA2 association is large in the full eligible sample and now shows very large direct effects in adenocarcinoma, Ky, and adherent contexts; external validation would distinguish robust replication from shared same-dataset structure or correlated genomic confounding. H48 is the next validation candidate after its context tests, and H13 would remain a later candidate. All conclusions remain associations in this dataset; unadjusted Welch comparisons can be confounded by correlated alterations, multiple testing is present, and no causal or broadly generalizable claim is made.",
  "research_notes": "Strong accepted dataset-specific associations now: H11 validated MSI-high/WRN; H12 accepted SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2, with adenocarcinoma H26, Ky H36, and adherent H40 direct effects all very large; H13 accepted KEAP1-loss/weaker NFE2L2, with adenocarcinoma H27, Ky H38, and adherent H41 direct effects very large. New major association: H48 TP53 loss/weaker USP7 dependency, +0.804 [0.783,0.825], accepted active; next step is context tests and independent validation. H36-H41 are accepted within-context confirmations, but they are not independent replication. H37 has only 27 Ky/MSI-high exposed cells, so interpret with caution despite huge lower bound. Validation requested now: H12. Next validation candidates: H48 if context tests remain consistent, then H13. Null/reject: H42 KRAS/RIT1. Deferred low priority: H43/H44 RIT1 interactions/mechanistic near null, H46 MYC/DHX9, H47 TP53/RPL11, plus prior ARID1A/SMARCA2 and KEAP1/USP7. RIT1 panel provides little support for upstream RTK-to-RAS/MAPK dependency modulation in this dataset. Maintain multiplicity caution, correlated-alteration confounding caution, and no causal/generalizability claims without validation.",
  "validate": "H12"
}

