  "narrative": "The delivered validation resolves the two due claims and completes the main independent-validation stage for the strongest associations. For H12, the independent validation R39 is signed +0.805 [0.775, 0.836] for the hypothesis that SMARCA4-loss cells have stronger SMARCA2 dependency, closely matching discovery R12 at +0.782 [0.761, 0.802]. Because the lower bound is far above any reasonable 10-percent practical benchmark and the direction and magnitude are replicated, I keep H12 accepted and close it as a dataset-specific association: SMARCA4-loss cells have stronger SMARCA2 dependency in this supplied dataset. For H13, the independent validation R65 is signed +0.804 [0.773, 0.835] for the refined hypothesis that KEAP1-loss cells have weaker NFE2L2 dependency, closely matching discovery R7 at +0.797 [0.776, 0.819]. This is very large and precisely estimated, so I accept and close H13. The signed direction means the raw KEAP1-loss minus KEAP1-non-loss difference is positive, i.e. less negative NFE2L2 scores and therefore weaker dependency. The opposite claim H7 is now explicitly rejected because the same validation strongly contradicts stronger NFE2L2 dependency in KEAP1-loss cells.\n\nThe supported core now consists of four independently replicated dataset-specific associations: MSI-high versus stronger WRN dependency (H11), SMARCA4-loss versus stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H12), TP53-loss versus weaker USP7 dependency (H48), and KEAP1-loss versus weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H13). Each has discovery and validation estimates near 0.8 with lower bounds well above the practical benchmark. Context-specific confirmations and null modifier checks reduce concern that these are simple artifacts of lineage, CRISPR library, culture, constructed marker assays, or tested co-alterations. For H13, adenocarcinoma, Ky-library, and adherent-culture direct effects are large and positive, whereas marker D, culture-interaction, and STK11 direct/interaction tests are null. For H48, context effects in adenocarcinoma, Ky-library, adherent culture, and MTAP-loss cells remain large; direct MTAP effects and MTAP-by-TP53 interaction do not support a dominant co-deletion explanation, although correlated 9p biology remains a caution.\n\nNegative and low-priority findings are scientifically useful. EGFR amplification did not replicate as a clinically meaningful dependency association in EGFR dependency (H4 failed validation). KRAS-mutation contrasts for KRAS, BRAF, EGFR, ERBB2, and RIT1 dependencies are mostly near null or imprecise. Many small effects involving MYC amplification, TP53 loss, MTAP loss, p53-pathway co-alterations, KIF18A, POLR2A, RPL11, DHX9, and receptor pathway markers remain below the practical benchmark or unresolved and should not be accepted. Constructed markers D/E/F behaved as null controls and should not be interpreted as biological pathways. The STK11 checks for NFE2L2 and KEAP1 were null; the MSI-high STK11 interaction was underpowered. The only borderline context modifier is H31, where the adherent-culture interaction for MSI-high versus WRN dependency is +0.114 [0.041, 0.187]. Its point estimate crosses the practical benchmark, but its lower bound does not, so it remains unresolved and does not overturn H11, whose main and adherent-culture effects remain enormous.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty is mainly residual confounding by correlated genomic alterations, underpowered subgroup interactions, and lack of causal or external-generalizability evidence. These results establish associations in the supplied dataset/validation structure, not mechanisms of dependency, not necessarily causal driver relationships, and not guaranteed clinical biomarker claims.\n\nThe most informative next analysis is to test specificity and modifiers of the validated core rather than pursue near-null small main effects. I prioritize the already active CDKN2A checks around p53 biology (H85/H86/H88), BRCA2/MSI DNA-repair selectivity tests (H73/H74/H83/H84), MYC amplification modification of the KEAP1-loss effect (H87), and receptor/PI3K/NF1 crosstalk tests (H77-H82). I also register two negative-control comparisons: KEAP1 loss versus WRN dependency and KEAP1 loss versus SMARCA2 dependency. These are expected to be null if the KEAP1 association is NFE2L2-selective; a large effect would indicate a broader dependency pattern and would require reevaluation of specificity.",
  "research_notes": "Validated core: H11 MSI-high -> stronger WRN; H12 SMARCA4-loss -> stronger SMARCA2; H48 TP53-loss -> weaker USP7; H13 KEAP1-loss -> weaker NFE2L2. Opposite H7 rejected. H13 validation R65 +0.804 [0.773,0.835]; context nulls: marker D H19/H23, culture H33, STK11 H69/H70. H31 culture interaction borderline +0.114 [0.041,0.187], unresolved deferred. Next priorities: H85/H86/H88 CDKN2A/p53 co-deletion checks; H73/H74/H83/H84 BRCA2/MSI DNA-repair specificity; H87 MYC interaction with KEAP1; H77-H82 PIK3CA/NF1/receptor crosstalk. New negative controls registered: KEAP1 loss vs WRN and KEAP1 loss vs SMARCA2, expected null; large effects would broaden interpretation. Treat all accepted claims as dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable."
