  "narrative": "The delivered validations require explicit reassessment. H48 reached its validation deadline: independent validation R52 is signed +0.799 with lower bound +0.768 and upper bound +0.831, closely matching discovery R38 at +0.804 with lower bound +0.783 and upper bound +0.825. Because the signed hypothesis direction is +1, the raw contrast is positive, meaning TP53-loss cells have less negative USP7 dependency scores and therefore weaker USP7 dependency. I keep H48 accepted and closed. H31 failed validation: discovery R59 suggested an adherent-culture interaction for MSI-high WRN dependency, signed +0.114 with 95 percent interval +0.041 to +0.187; independent validation R78 is only +0.0236 with interval -0.0865 to +0.1338, spanning zero, clinically trivial, and opposite directions. I reject H31 and close it as unsupported context modification, while preserving H11 and H39 main effects. H55 also fails validation: discovery R48 +0.0090 and validation R79 +0.0126 are near zero; I reject it. The independently supported core remains: H11 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; H12 SMARCA4-loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H48 TP53-loss -> weaker USP7 dependency; H13 KEAP1-loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency. Each has discovery and validation estimates near 0.80 with lower bounds far above the practical absolute benchmark and far above any plausible 10 percent threshold in arbitrary dependency units. Subgroup analyses in adenocarcinoma, Ky library, adherent culture, and ARID1A-loss contexts remain large where tested, whereas Cas9-high, library, lineage, culture, marker D/E/F, and most co-alteration interactions are small. I additionally closed a batch of completed negative same-dataset checks because their point estimates are small, intervals include zero, and validation is not warranted: H1 KRAS mutation vs KRAS dependency, H6 ERBB2 amplification vs ERBB2 dependency, H43 and H44 RIT1 pathway checks, H10 H46 and H55 MYC-amplification checks, H56 and H47 TP53-loss checks on KIF18A and RPL11, H58 and H59 MTAP-loss p53 co-alteration checks, H34 ARID1A direct chromatin control, H35 KEAP1-to-USP7 cross-check, and H14 H16 H20 H29 H30 context interactions. These negative findings are useful because they show the core associations are not explained by broad receptor, MYC, MTAP, ARID1A, constructed-marker, or most technical/context effects. Unresolved scientific uncertainty remains for active no-evidence specificity and pathway tests, especially direct STK11-loss on WRN and SMARCA2 H99 and H100, BRCA2-loss on DHX9 POLR2A and KIF18A H73 H74 and H83, PIK3CA NF1 and ERBB2 crosstalk H77 through H82 and H93 and H94, MDM2 co-alteration checks H75 H86 and H50, and ARID1A interaction H72. These results are associations in the supplied dataset and validation splits, not causal driver relationships or externally generalizable clinical biomarkers.",
